# ReelRank environment variables
#
# BOTH are optional. Copy to `.env` only if you need to change a default:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# There are no secrets required to run this project. The default build is fully
# synthetic and self-contained, which is deliberate -- a reviewer should be able
# to clone, build and serve without registering for anything.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: build the catalog from the real YouTube Data API instead of the
# synthetic generator. Free key, no billing:
#   https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/getting-started
#
# Affects the CATALOG ONLY. Watch histories stay simulated either way -- no
# public dataset of real YouTube watch logs exists (see docs/DATASET.md).
# Used by src/recsys/data/youtube_api.py; without it the build falls back to
# synthetic and records that fallback in data/processed/data_meta.json.
#
#   YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_key_here
#   python scripts/build_all.py --source youtube_api
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: port for the API server. Falls back to `serving.port` in
# config.yaml (7860). Most PaaS hosts set this for you.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=7860

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: any config.yaml value can be overridden with a RECSYS__ prefix,
# nesting expressed as double underscores. Useful for tuning a running
# container without rebuilding it. See load_config() in src/recsys/config.py.
#
#   RECSYS__POLICY__MMR_LAMBDA=0.5      -> policy.mmr_lambda
#   RECSYS__SERVING__DEFAULT_N=12       -> serving.default_n
#   RECSYS__PROJECT__REFERENCE_DATE=2026-01-01   -> pins the build clock
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
